  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Host Communities: Creating Accessible Conditions for Population Evacuation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtRokada is a CCCM and Protection partner, who currently has established presence in 15 oblasts with experienced and trained staff. All project activities were designed taking into consideration the specific needs of vulnerable groups, including women, children, older people, and people with disabilities to ensure the centrality of the protection.ltbrgtRokada will support authorities in 6 oblasts to create 1250 new spaces in 22&#xA0;sites, including 372&#xA0;spaces for people with limited mobility. This will be complemented with transportation component and response to the social care facilities. In addition, Rokada will supplement this project with case management protective measures, social support, and psychological support at the expense of other funding.ltbrgtThe project aims to enhance reception and accommodation conditions for newly evacuated populations in collective sites, prioritizing accessibility, safety, and inclusivity. The approach includes two main components: ensuring adequate capacity and standards in existing and new accommodation spaces and providing essential Camp Coordination and Camp Management (CCCM) services alongside emergency support. Accessibility upgrades and targeted repairs will ensure inclusivity for individuals with disabilities and limited mobility. Rokada will work closely with local authorities to expand capacity through repairs and upgrades, ensuring effective evacuation-to- settlement pathways for vulnerable groups. Complementary coordination with the Protection Cluster will ensure comprehensive support, emphasizing low-mobility and high-need individuals throughout the process.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
